<!--Post: 4838--><!--Time: 1106769151-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4838"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lakesguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lakesguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some people theorized, before his reappearance, that BTK was either a student or a professor at Wichita State so his class schedule could have been M-W-F with Tuesdays and Thursdays off. I think that&#39;s one possibility that the original group of FBI profilers came up with back in the late 1970&#39;s. Don&#39;t know if anyone still thinks that&#39;s possible. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
