<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4964"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10745103.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10745103.htm</a> <BR>Posted on Thu, Jan. 27, 2005  <BR>POLICE TO TALK TODAY ABOUT CASE <BR>More BTK victims?  <BR> <BR>A possible clue found near Valley Center focuses speculation on 2 unsolved homicides in areas north of Wichita <BR> <BR>BY TIM POTTER AND HURST LAVIANA <BR> <BR>The Wichita Eagle <BR>================================================== <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/10745102.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/10745102.htm</a> <BR>Posted on Thu, Jan. 27, 2005 <BR>POSSIBLE BTK CONNECTIONS <BR>April 27, 1985 -- Park City resident Marine Hedge is abducted. Her car is found May 2 at 21st and Woodlawn; her purse is found May 5 near 143rd East and 37th North; her body is found May 5, 1985, near 53rd North and Webb Road. <BR> <BR>Jan. 19, 1991 -- Delores Davis abducted from her home one-half mile east of Park City. Her body is found Feb. 1, 1991, near 117th North and Meridian. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4964-->
<!--Post: 4966--><!--Time: 1106842219-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4966"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the Anna Williams thing was a Friday or Saturday night...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4966-->
<!--Post: 5143--><!--Time: 1106924261-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5143"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 6:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that the letter “T” in any of the days of the week might be a factor in the case, Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
